quran[21]{c,v,t}:
  44,19,"And do not rebel against Allah. Indeed, I have come to you with a manifest authority."
  44,20,"I seek refuge in my Lord and your Lord, lest you should stone me (to death)."
  44,21,"If you do not believe me, keep away from me.’"
  44,22,"Then he called upon his Lord, saying: ‘These are indeed guilty people.’"
  44,23,"(Allah told him:) ‘Set out with My servants by night, for you will indeed be pursued."
  44,24,Then leave the sea split open; they are certainly an army bound to drown.’
  44,25,"How many gardens and springs did they leave behind,"
  44,26,"and green fields and magnificent buildings,"
  44,27,"and luxuries, in which they rejoiced!"
  44,28,"So it was, and We gave it (all) to other people as an inheritance."
  44,29,"Then neither the heaven wept over them nor the earth, nor were they granted respite."
  44,30,"And verily, We delivered the Children of Israel from the humiliating punishment,"
  44,31,"from Pharaoh. Indeed, he was a rebel among the transgressors."
  44,32,"Indeed, We chose them knowingly above all the (contemporary) nations."
  44,33,We gave them some signs wherein there was a clear test.
  44,34,"Indeed, these (Meccans) say:"
  44,35,"‘There is nothing except our first death, and we shall not be resurrected."
  44,36,"Bring our fathers (back to life), if you are truthful.’"
  44,37,"Are they better or the people of Tubba‘* and those who were before them? We destroyed them. Indeed, they were evildoers."
  44,38,We did not create the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them for play.
  44,39,We only created them both with a genuine reason. But most of them do not know.
